with independent error processes tηtu and tϵtu. If the system matrices do not evolve with time, the state-space model
is called time-invariant or time-homogeneous. If the disturbances ϵt and initial state vector α1 are assumed to have
a normal distribution, then the model is termed Gaussian. Further, if GtHJ
